            <ArticleTitle>A pagetic elderly lady with back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/ageing/afn041</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An elderly lady suffering from Paget's disease presented with severe back pain after sustaining a fall. The rise in inflammatory markers and poor response to analgesics led to the diagnosis of septic discitis [corrected] that was confirmed by MRI. A high index of suspicion for septic discitis [corrected] is necessary in elderly patients presenting with back pain and an associated rise in inflammatory markers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
